 "notes": [
  "This is the existing .sylvia-gm-campaign ZIP contract: authority.jsonl, blobs/<sha256>, then canonical manifest.json in exact member order.",
  "The manifest schema is structural. The codec remains authoritative for exact product/schema generations, migration provenance, table names and row schemas, canonical bytes, ordering, limits, hashes, counts, and closure indexes.",
  "Every non-manifest member is declared by exact name, size, and SHA-256; every retained package blob must agree with authority rows and package-file byte counts.",
  "Exports contain the selected campaign aggregate and exact package closure. They exclude Full Audit, credentials, independent Builder chats, unrelated campaigns, and workspace scratch.",
  "Recovery verifies into staging before the sole authority writer commits it; retrieving this definition does not export, recover, or inspect campaign data.",
  "This is the already-supported format 2, selected only when saved thinking is explicitly included. The provider-private.jsonl member is required and checked by the existing private-record codec; it is excluded from ordinary history. Format 1 excludes this member. No credentials or Full Audit are included in either format."
 ],
